      "claim": "Knowledge of prime numbers is not a prerequisite for performing typical actuarial tasks such as risk modeling, life‑table calculations, or financial valuation.",
      "evidence": "Actuarial exam syllabi (e.g., SOA Exam P, FM, IFM) focus on probability, calculus, financial mathematics, and statistics; they contain no explicit requirement to understand prime numbers.",
